---
kind: scene
id: pier.theo.reed
title: Green reed, not brown
on: placeVisit
target: place.pier
after: 'visited("pier.theo.meet")'
when: 'holds("present", ["theo", "pier"]) && !run.lantern.frame'
priority: 15
---

## The reed beds behind the pier

::bg{location="reed_beds" time="morning"}
::actor{character="theo" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
::set{run.seen.theo = run.day}
@theo{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: Qualified hands came back.
@narrator{code="0010"}: He has a bundle of green reed already cut and tied with fishing line, as if he knew.
@theo{code="0020"}: Soak it tonight. Bend it tomorrow. If you bend it dry, it cracks, and then you cry, and then Pell laughs at you.
::set{run.lantern.frame = true}
::set{run.aff.theo += 1}

<match subject="run.day">
  <when is="..2">
    @theo{code="0030" emotion="shy"}: Hey. Wednesday night, low tide, the water off the lighthouse does a thing. Glows. It only happens a few nights a summer.
    @theo{code="0040" emotion="shy"}: I go every year. By myself, usually.
    <branch id="lighthouseAsk" prompt="Theo is suddenly very interested in his knife.">
      <choice id="yes" text="“Wednesday night. I'll be there.”">
        ::accept{quest="theoLighthouse"}
        @theo{code="0050" emotion="happy"}: Bring a jumper. It's cold at the top.
      </choice>
      <choice id="no" text="“I'll probably be gluing things.”">
        @theo{code="0060" emotion="sad"}: Right. Yeah. Lanterns.
      </choice>
    </branch>
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @theo{code="0070"}: Festival's close. Don't let the frame get rained on.
  </otherwise>
</match>

::actor{character="theo" action="fadeOut"}
